course: dictionary
lesson: 4307
title: Grizzly: a bear, a colour, and a grump
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: When you meet a new word, read the words around it. They are its context, and they leave clues. «A grizzly at a waterfall in autumn snaps up leaping salmon to get fat before winter.» Waterfall, salmon and fat before winter all point to a large animal that catches fish, so a grizzly is a big animal.
explain: Grizzly can also be a describing word. «A grizzly old man sat by the fire.» A man cannot be a bear, so ask what fits. The word old and the word man tell you that grizzly means grey-haired here.
explain: Words can change meaning in different places. In UK speech, «The grizzly baby would not stop whining» is about a baby who is grumpy, not a bear. The whining is the clue. When context is not enough, a dictionary settles it.
fact: A grizzly bear is a large brown bear of North America.
fact: A grizzly bear has a hump on its shoulders and fur tipped with grey.
fact: «Grizzly» can describe something grey or grey-haired, as in «a grizzly old man».
fact: In UK informal speech, a grizzly baby or child is grumpy and whiny.
fact: Most bears eat almost anything: berries, nuts, roots, insects, fish and meat. A grizzly at a waterfall may catch salmon to get fat before winter.
exercise: «The grizzly bear caught a leaping salmon at the waterfall.» What is a grizzly bear? | *A large brown bear of North America | A small grey bird | A type of tree | A kind of fish
exercise: «The grizzly old man sat by the fire with white hair.» What does grizzly mean here? | *Grey or grey-haired | Brown and furry | Angry and loud | Very large
exercise: «The grizzly baby would not stop whining.» In UK speech, what does grizzly mean? | Happy and giggling | Sleepy | Hungry for fish | *Grumpy and whiny
test: «A grizzly has a hump on its shoulders and grey-tipped fur.» Which feature shows it is a grizzly? | *A hump on its shoulders | Spots | Wings | Long tail
test: «Most bears eat almost anything: berries, nuts, roots, insects, fish and meat.» What does almost suggest? | Only plants | *Nearly everything, but not quite every single thing | Only meat | Nothing at all
exam: «Polar bears and grizzlies have met in Canada and had pizzly cubs.» Which two animals met and had cubs together? | Two sloths | Grizzly and salmon | Two harpy eagles | *Polar bear and grizzly
